packetFunc1(a,b,c)
    a[0] is the current packet number. the rest is probably some xor weird stuff.

    b is very probably packet data.
    c is the length of the entire packet.

    chat message length 60:
        you can set a breakpoint with $var2.value == 64 to break on this packet.
        c = 64
        b = hex[4D FE 3C 00, ... 60 characters of chat message]
        b = dec[77 254 60 0, ... 60 characters of chat message]
    chat message length 59:
        c = 63
        b = hex[4D FE 3B 00, ... 59 characters of chat message]
        b = dec[77 254 59 0, ... 59 characters of chat message]

    those length 7 packets that get sent a lot, ping related?:
        c = 1
        b = hex[70]
        b = dec[112]